1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:02,580
(Trying Hard To Understand the Rules)

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:04,720
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:06,520
Whoever is pointed at stands up.

4
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:07,320
Okay?

5
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:07,680
Okay.

6
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:08,680
What's the chant again?

7
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,200
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

8
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,280
(Memorizing the chant)
How many dances?

9
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:12,520
Say, three dances, for example.

10
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:13,320
Then point to someone.

11
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,480
Make sure it's clear
who you're pointing at.

12
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:16,160
Which word is the "dance"
in "three dances"?

13
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:17,020
"Dance" as in dancing.

14
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:17,620
(How many dances)

15
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:18,180
(Dance as in dancing)

16
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:18,700
(When to point)

17
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:20,920
(Do we need to stand up)

18
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:22,480
Come on, you go first.

19
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:23,120
I'll point.

20
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,600
I'll say, How many dances
does the Natural High crew know,

21
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:27,080
and you say...

22
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:27,880
One dance.

23
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:30,560
Just once.

24
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:31,800
That's an instant elimination.

25
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,840
(Game referee)
You're out.

26
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:33,240
Go.

27
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:36,640
The cap is three.

28
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:38,280
The cap is three, right?

29
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:39,200
It's eight.

30
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:40,360
The cap is eight?

31
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:42,200
We need to dance eight times?

32
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,000
Right.

33
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:44,680
I didn't get it.

34
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,120
I thought cha-cha-cha was just one.

35
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:48,200
Isn't this just like that monkey game?

36
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:48,960
How many monkeys?

37
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:50,840
Right.

38
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:51,880
After they finish their cha-cha,

39
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:53,160
the next person calls it out, right?

40
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:53,760
Yes.

41
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,640
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

42
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:56,280
No.

43
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:57,120
(Rule explainer is online)
After you ask,

44
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:58,520
so if she says two dances...

45
00:00:58,520 --> 00:00:59,280
Two dances.

46
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:00,320
(Us?)
Then it's those two.

47
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:01,540
(Guess we gotta stand up)

48
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:02,560
Cha, cha.

49
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,400
And then you ask.

50
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,200
(My turn again?)
Then you say.

51
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,440
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

52
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:07,280
One dance.

53
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:09,620
(Got it now)
Cha.

54
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,000
(Seems to get it now)
Then I ask next, right?

55
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,120
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

56
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:14,080
Two dances.

57
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:15,360
Cha, cha.

58
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:17,760
(Sort of get it)
I won't point anymore?

59
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:18,880
Yes, the next person points.

60
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:19,760
Oh.

61
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:20,480
Cha, cha.

62
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,640
Only the first person who asks,

63
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:23,200
asks and points at the same time, right?

64
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:23,800
The first person asks,

65
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:24,600
the second person points.

66
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:26,280
The person who asks
doesn't even need to stand.

67
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:27,560
They just continue the line.

68
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:28,680
Right.

69
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:29,760
(Caught the keyword "no need to stand")
Then I can just keep asking.

70
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:30,560
Sure.

71
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:33,000
(That doesn't sound right)
Well, then nobody's gonna point at you.

72
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:34,480
Makes sense.

73
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:38,020
(Dancing Yak, Extra Edition)

74
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:39,320
This mission is called,

75
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:40,480
Dancing Yak.

76
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:44,220
(Dancing Yak, Extra Edition)

77
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,640
Is this the movement?

78
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:55,800
Of course.

79
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,960
Which movement are we supposed to copy?

80
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,000
This one?

81
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:02,580
(Confirming the movement)

82
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,480
Okay, everyone else put your glasses on.

83
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:06,580
(Looking for the target)

84
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:07,680
Where is everyone?

85
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,940
(Can't find the target anywhere)

86
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,080
Where is she?

87
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:14,120
I lost her.

88
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:15,640
Over here.

89
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:19,020
(Disastrous start)

90
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,100
(here we go again)

91
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,460
(The chase begins)

92
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,800
Why did you stand up, Bai?

93
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,280
Does this count as one lap?

94
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,680
No, you have to go
from here and come back.

95
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,620
(Humankind reverting to wild ancestors)

96
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,800
I just saw what you'll look like
when you're old.

97
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:46,020
(That was spot on)

98
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:49,860
(Looking a bit stiff)

99
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:52,680
Where's my chair?

100
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:54,380
(Searching for the chair)

101
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:55,560
(Still moving slowly)

102
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:56,760
Where even am I?

103
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,000
Plateau.

104
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,260
(Snagged a seat)

105
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,880
Time to watch Bai's dance moves.

106
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:03,720
Bring it on.

107
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,520
Okay, let's go with this one.

108
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,680
Didn't see that coming, Bai.

109
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:19,120
Is this the move?

110
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:21,080
(Confirming the move)

111
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,080
Everyone else put your glasses on.

112
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:26,900
(Searching for the target)

113
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:28,580
(Search failed)

114
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:33,060
(Locked eyes,
but you're not the one I'm looking for)

115
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,040
Don't bump into me by mistake.

116
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:39,700
(Then it's gotta be you)

117
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,260
(Unbelievable)

118
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:49,500
(What's going on here?)

119
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,000
You gotta go behind the chair.

120
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,840
Chase him.
Who are you even ambushing here?

121
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,200
How can you be so clueless?

122
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:01,060
(Switching to a counter-chase strategy)

123
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,560
You can go in reverse too?

124
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,100
Yes.

125
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:05,420
(Realization hits)
You can go in reverse too?

126
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,320
Niu Lai.

127
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:10,200
Mom!

128
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:11,240
You gotta loop around.

129
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:11,760
Loop around.

130
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:18,260
(Snagged a seat)

131
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:21,520
Are you looking at me?

132
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,640
Nice one.

133
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:27,100
(Dancing Chengcheng)

134
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,540
(Dancing Yak)
Alright, guys.

135
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,200
How are you supposed to disco?

136
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:38,660
(Nailed it)

137
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:44,280
Here we go.

138
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,580
I didn't touch you.

139
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:50,800
(Not my intention)
Accidental bump.

140
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:51,320
Sorry.

141
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:57,980
(Defense mode)

142
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:04,820
(Sneak attack)

143
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:07,420
(How dare you fake me out)

144
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,140
(Sprinting off the scene)

145
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:14,620
(Snagged a seat)

146
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:16,080
He sat back down?

147
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:16,940
(Can't believe it)

148
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:22,060
(Nonstop Cha-Cha-Cha)

149
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:24,820
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

150
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:25,720
Come on.

151
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:27,180
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

152
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,560
One dance.

153
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,280
Cha.

154
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:32,740
(Almost messed up)

155
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:34,340
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

156
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,400
(Pointing at Mr. Huang)
Three dances.

157
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:37,480
Cha.

158
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:39,700
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

159
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:40,800
(Pointing at Wang Anyu)
Four dances.

160
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,800
Cha.

161
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:46,700
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

162
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:48,040
(Pointing at Mr. Huang)
Six dances.

163
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:51,600
Cha.

164
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:55,540
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

165
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,800
Six dances.

166
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:02,880
Cha.

167
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:09,740
(Showcase
of the Natural High crew's dance moves)

168
00:06:10,740 --> 00:06:11,620
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

169
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:12,840
You again.

170
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:15,240
(Being the starter feels pretty good)

171
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,720
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

172
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,840
Six dances.

173
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:22,520
(Loving every second)
Cha.

174
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:28,940
(How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?)

175
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,400
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

176
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,360
Six dances.

177
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,060
(Already predicted by Hu)

178
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,560
Cha.

179
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:35,980
(Bai has gone totally wild)

180
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:37,600
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

181
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:38,440
(Cheng is eliminated)
Five dances.

182
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:41,240
Cha

183
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,000
(Still loving every second)

184
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,120
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

185
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:44,840
Five dances.

186
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,920
Cha.

187
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:50,260
(Best front-row seat)

188
00:06:50,260 --> 00:06:52,000
(I'll watch with you)

189
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,320
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

190
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:54,400
Two dances.

191
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:55,800
Cha.

192
00:06:56,180 --> 00:06:57,800
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

193
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:58,560
Four dances.

194
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,960
Cha.

195
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:03,500
(Two more joined the best viewing spot)

196
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:04,760
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

197
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:05,560
(Directing it back at Bai)
One dance.

198
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:08,240
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

199
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,040
Three dances.

200
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:12,960
How many dances
does the Natural High crew know?

201
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:13,600
One dance.

202
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:18,020
(Wait, you can do that?)

203
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:21,020
(Dancing Yak, Folk Dance Showcase)

204
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:22,000
Come on, Bing.

205
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,680
Let's do a folk dance chase.

206
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:32,100
(Messing with him)

207
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:37,620
(A classic feint)

208
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:50,780
(The back-and-forth begins)

209
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:53,940
(Come here)

210
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:57,800
Come on.

211
00:07:58,400 --> 00:07:59,600
Catch me if you can.

212
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,700
(Taunting non-stop)

213
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,040
Fei Yangyang, you...
[*A cartoon character]

214
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:11,820
(Snagged a seat)

215
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:12,640
It's way too far.

216
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:13,520
Feels like I can't reach it.

217
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:16,900
(Teng Explaining
Drop the Handkerchief Rules to Hu)

218
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:18,880
Doesn't Teng kinda like Qiang?

219
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:20,760
Who's Qiang?

220
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:22,280
What was her hit song again?

221
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,440
That...

222
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:25,280
"Don't Ask Me What Disco Is".

223
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,200
Zhang Qiang.

224
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:27,920
Teng, the only difference between you
and Zhang Qiang right now

225
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:28,920
is a bit of eyeshadow.

226
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:29,480
Is there...

227
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,560
Churan, got any eyeshadow in your bag?

228
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:32,080
Slap a couple of swipes on him.

229
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:33,580
(Taking a closer look)

230
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:35,080
Gotta get some hair clips too.

231
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:37,000
(Vision completely blocked)
I legit can't see a thing.

232
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:37,960
(Helpful bystander)
I'll clip it for you.

233
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:55,760
This game is just like
Drop the Handkerchief.

234
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:56,680
(Puzzled)
Is it the same thing

235
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:57,720
as dodgeball?

236
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:58,640
(No no no)
That's completely different.

237
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:01,960
Drop the Handkerchief is when
everyone sits in a circle like this,

238
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:04,520
then someone holds
a handkerchief running behind,

239
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:06,800
and quietly drops it

240
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:07,560
behind someone's back.

241
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:08,960
(Memory unlocked)
That person has to notice,

242
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:09,760
and then chase you down.

243
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,520
(Passionate singing)
♪Don't anybody tell him♪

244
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:13,640
Wait, no.

245
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:14,880
(Memory fading again)
I was starting to get it,

246
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,200
and you just sang me
into confusion again.

247
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:17,080
The song goes like,

248
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,920
(Reciting version)
gently place it behind a little friend.

249
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:19,640
So we gotta,

250
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:21,560
like sing while playing?

251
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:22,180
(Not really)

252
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,040
But nobody's allowed to tell him.

253
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,320
♪Drop, drop♪

254
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:28,080
(Searching for memories)
♪Drop the handkerchief!♪

255
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:31,440
♪Gently place it behind a little friend♪

256
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,760
♪Don't anybody tell him♪

257
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:34,840
I don't think I really played

258
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,240
Drop the Handkerchief as a kid.

259
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:38,900
(Off-The-Cuff Brainstorm
on Wang Bu Liu Xing)

260
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:40,960
(Tall Tale King)
While the Tall Tale Team reads the card,

261
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:42,200
the Guessing Team can share

262
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:44,440
(Wang bu liu xing)
your thoughts on wang bu liu xing.

263
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:45,880
It doesn't have to be an idiom, right?

264
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:47,000
Not necessarily.

265
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,960
(Starting the tall tale)
This guy named Wang stayed at a hotel.

266
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:50,200
No, it used to be liu xing.
[*Trendy]

267
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:51,480
Now it's not.

268
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:53,340
(Wang bu liu xing)

269
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:54,480
Wang

270
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:56,240
is an old-school phrasing.

271
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:58,080
We say da bu liu xing nowadays.
[*Walking fast]

272
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,820
(W? w?)

273
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,480
Is he talking about Qin Shi Huang?

274
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:04,000
It might have punctuation marks too.

275
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:05,900
Wang doesn't stay, fine.

276
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:10,020
